  "question": {
    "text": "The co-ordinate of a point on the auxiliary circle of the ellipse $x^{2}+2 y^{2}=4$ corresponding to the point on the ellipse whose eccentric angle is $60^{\\circ}$ will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "7LsZV",
      "text": "$(\\sqrt{3}, 1)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0P8oP",
      "text": "$(1, \\sqrt{3})$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0vYXL",
      "text": "$(1,1)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0HmwX",
      "text": "$(1,2)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{x^{2}}{4}+\\frac{y^{2}}{2}=1$\r\nEquation of auxiliary circle is\r\n$x^{2}+y^{2}=4$\r\n$\\therefore$ Point on the auxiliary circle is\r\n$\\begin{array}{l}\r\np\\left(2 \\cos 60^{\\circ}, 2 \\sin 60^{\\circ}\\right) \\\\\r\np(1, \\sqrt{3})\r\n\\end{array}$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/nfCjUhotOOM8Mb6Tih9Uke8GcDyN2Db2TF1KWjuRwOo.original.fullsize.png\">",
